Q: PUBNUB here_now returning wrong channel list A: <p>2026 update: this thread uses the old PubNub JavaScript 3.x API. If you are coming here with v12, the code is quite different now.</p>
<p>The 2015 behavior was a bit nasty. <code>PUBNUB.init()</code> returned the PubNub instance configured with your keys, but the code in the question later calls <code>PUBNUB.here_now()</code> on the global <code>PUBNUB</code> object. That global reference used the default <code>demo</code> keys, which explains why you could suddenly see a huge number of channels and occupants that were not yours.</p>
<p>Craig Conover from PubNub confirmed this behavior in the comments on the inital answer.</p>
<p>In v12 you keep the PubNub instance you create:</p>
<pre><code>const pubnub = new PubNub({
  publishKey: &quot;your-publish-key&quot;,
  subscribeKey: &quot;your-subscribe-key&quot;,
  userId: &quot;user-123&quot;
});
</code></pre>
<p>For the question here, if you have two channels and want to see who is currently on them, ask for these two channels directly:</p>
<pre><code>const result = await pubnub.hereNow({
  channels: [&quot;channel-1&quot;, &quot;channel-2&quot;],
  includeUUIDs: true
});

console.log(result);
</code></pre>
<p><code>hereNow()</code> gives you occupancy for the channels you requested. It is not an API for listing every channel connected with your keyset.</p>
<p>There is also a slightly different case. If what you actually need is &quot;which channels is this user currently on?&quot;, use <code>whereNow()</code>:</p>
<pre><code>const result = await pubnub.whereNow({
  uuid: &quot;user-123&quot;
});
</code></pre>
<p>Presence needs to be enabled for the keyset.</p>
<p>Current Presence docs:<br />
<a href="https://www.pubnub.com/docs/sdks/javascript/api-reference/presence" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.pubnub.com/docs/sdks/javascript/api-reference/presence</a></p>
<p>JavaScript SDK configuration:<br />
<a href="https://www.pubnub.com/docs/sdks/javascript/api-reference/configuration" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.pubnub.com/docs/sdks/javascript/api-reference/configuration</a></p>
<p>So for the old SDK, the accepted answer found the right cause. For current PubNub JavaScript, there is no need to deal with that old global <code>PUBNUB</code> pattern. Keep the instance created with <code>new PubNub(...)</code> and run <code>hereNow()</code> on it.</p>
<p>Disclosure: I work at PubNub.</p>
